From 919d22f3ada07188156e2d12a542dcc9fe7cb906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 22:55:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/29] fix(julia): stop rounding julia's un-frounded scalar
 uniforms to float32

Root cause, same class as 28c4a80 but in a different place: julia is
dispatched through a hand-authored typed-emitter body
(emit_typed_cpp.py's _render_julia_body), independent of the generic
ABI-driven bind path that commit fixed. Its bind_synth_julia_julia
constructor literal still wrapped 11 of julia's 12 scalar float
uniforms (cReal, cImag, centerX, centerY, rotation, stripeFreq,
lightAngle, cSpeed, cRadius, zoomSpeed, zoomDepth) in
noisemaker::f32(...) before storing them as double -- rounding to
float32 at bind time a value the JS authority's createCanonicalBindings
(glsl-kernel.js) never rounds (it explicitly Math.fround()s only
seed/aspectRatio/aspect/time/globalTime/deltaTime, spreading every
ordinary effect parameter, including julia's, untouched). Only `time`
is a genuine reserved name for julia and keeps its f32() wrap.

Verified against a direct, independent invocation of the live JS
authority's juliaFactory via bindCanonicalKernel/createCanonicalBindings
with the exact iterations-clamp-1001 case bindings: real value is
0x3f56a8fe, confirming the previously pinned oracle expectation
(0x3f56a8ef) was itself computed under the same over-rounding
assumption, not the fix. Fixed the emitter template and regenerated
typed_slice.cpp/typed_manifest.json via the real generator (no hand
patch to generated files).

Full 208-effect float32-lane sweep (seed 20260916): synth/julia goes
from divergent (15/23668 values, e.g. iterations-clamp-1001 pixel
0.395751953125 vs 0.3955078125) to 0 divergent, alongside
filter/hs, synth/mandelbrot and synth/noise (already fixed by the
merged 28c4a80). Native: 586 PASS, 1 pre-existing unrelated FAIL
(classic_noise oracle metadata pin, present since ca68fc4). Frozen
166-record corpus parity lane: 100% byte-exact.

Also repairs the julia-parity oracle package's own self-authentication,
found stale while re-deriving ground truth for the fix above:
- julia_oracle_generator.mjs's pinned CPU import-closure was missing
  src/effects/adapters/remap.js entirely and had 3 stale hashes for
  index.js/canonical-kernels.js/upstream-snapshot.js (unrelated
  additions to the authority -- median.js/snow.js adapters -- shifted
  these after the package was last frozen). Re-derived against the
  current, correctly-mounted, immutable authority checkout.
- The SAME staleness mirrored in
  generate_julia_native_oracle_include.py's EXPECTED_CLOSURE, plus a
  stale pinned upstream shader revision (117a236... -> 0ed489ec...) in
  both files.
- The generator's own render() helper independently baked in the exact
  same over-frounding bug being fixed above (it Math.fround()'d
  cReal/cImag/centerX/centerY/rotation/stripeFreq/lightAngle/cSpeed/
  cRadius/zoomSpeed/zoomDepth before calling bindCanonicalKernel), so
  the oracle's own frozen expectations were computed under the same
  wrong assumption. Fixed render() to stop frounding those 11 fields,
  regenerated the whole package end to end (JSON -> report -> native
  .inc include) via --write, and updated the 12 cascading pinned
  digests this changed (1 case digest + 11 mutation-ledger digests, all
  for iterations-clamp-1001 -- the only one of 18 frozen cases whose
  precise, non-round-number bindings actually cross a rounding
  threshold under the fix). tests.test_julia_oracle: 7/7 PASS (was
  2 FAIL from the stale pins before any of this).

Unrelated hardening found and fixed along the way: src/effects/snow.cpp
used std::sin/std::cos/std::pow (platform libm) instead of this
project's verified-bit-exact noisemaker::fdlibm::sin/cos/pow, the
convention every other file in the codebase follows. Durable fix
regardless of outcome; empirically did not change filter/snow's own
remaining 192-pixel divergence in the v17 sweep case (confirmed
bit-for-bit identical before/after) -- that root cause is still open.

Also open, diagnosed but not fixed: synth/gradient, synth/mandala,
synth/pattern, synth/sacredGeometry show the vector-typed analogue of
this same bug class (ordinary vec2/vec3/vec4 DSL parameters, e.g.
gradient's color1-4, are bound as raw un-rounded JS doubles by the
authority's parseColor() but narrowed to float32 (glsl::Vec3) at
uniform-bind time in the C++ port). A naive widen-the-storage-type fix
(glsl::Vec3 -> glsl::DVec3, generalizing the existing narrowly-scoped
_CLASSIC_NOISEDECK_DOUBLE_PALETTE_CARRIERS mechanism) does not work:
the generic typed emitter infers local-variable and return types from
the GLSL type alone, not from the referenced uniform's actual C++
type, so the narrowing just moves to the next local-variable assignment
(and several call sites don't even compile, lacking an implicit
Vec3(DVec3) conversion). A correct fix needs the emitter to propagate
double precision through the specific subset of each expression graph
that traces back to one of these uniforms -- reverted the incomplete
attempt rather than leave the tree broken or ship an unverified change.

